Drill 7 — Strategic Customer Momentum Classification
Exact task statement
Classify significant customers as accelerating, stable, softening, or sharply declining using recent revenue trend.
Build order
25.	Calculate trailing_12m_revenue by customer.
26.	Calculate last_3m_revenue and prior_3m_revenue.
27.	Compute momentum amount and momentum percent.
28.	Apply a documented momentum classification rule.
Validation checks
•	last_3m and prior_3m windows must not overlap.
•	Momentum buckets must be mutually exclusive.
•	Handle zero prior-period revenue safely.
Final output template
customer_code	oracle_customer_name	top_150_flag	trailing_12m_revenue	last_3m_revenue	prior_3m_revenue	momentum_amt	momentum_pct	momentum_status
100234	Customer A	Yes	48200000	13400000	11100000	2300000	20.7%	Accelerating
Output column definitions
•	momentum_amt = last_3m_revenue - prior_3m_revenue.
•	momentum_pct = momentum_amt / prior_3m_revenue.
•	momentum_status = classification based on thresholds you define and keep consistent.

--====================================================================================================
With cte_1 as
(Select
	customer_code,
	oracle_customer_name,
	top150_mapping,
	amount,
	rev_mth_dt,
	is_trailing_12m,
	is_trailing_3m,
	is_prior_3m
From platinum.txn_normalized t
Left Join platinum.period_reference p
On t.rev_mth_dt = p.month_start
Where top150_mapping = 'Yes'
Order by t.rev_mth_dt Desc
),
cte_2 as
(Select 
	distinct customer_code,
	oracle_customer_name,
	top150_mapping,
	sum(amount) over(partition by customer_code) as customer_ttm_rev
From cte_1
Where is_trailing_12m = 1
Group by
	customer_code,
	oracle_customer_name,
	top150_mapping,
	amount
),
cte_3 as
(Select 
	distinct customer_code,
	oracle_customer_name,
	top150_mapping,
	sum(amount) over(partition by customer_code) as customer_t3m_rev
From cte_1
Where is_trailing_3m = 1
Group by
	customer_code,
	oracle_customer_name,
	top150_mapping,
	amount
),
cte_4 as
(Select 
	distinct customer_code,
	oracle_customer_name,
	top150_mapping,
	sum(amount) over(partition by customer_code) as customer_p3m_rev
From cte_1
Where is_prior_3m = 1
Group by
	customer_code,
	oracle_customer_name,
	top150_mapping,
	amount
)
Select
	distinct c2.customer_code,
	c2.oracle_customer_name,
	c2.top150_mapping,
	c2.customer_ttm_rev,
	c3.customer_t3m_rev,
	c4.customer_p3m_rev,
	Coalesce((c3.customer_t3m_rev - c4.customer_p3m_rev),0) as momentum_amt,
	Round(((c3.customer_t3m_rev - c4.customer_p3m_rev) / nullif(c4.customer_p3m_rev,0))*100,2) as momentum_pct,
	Case
		When Round(((c3.customer_t3m_rev - c4.customer_p3m_rev) / nullif(c4.customer_p3m_rev,0))*100,2) >= 5
		Then 'Accelerating'
		When Round(((c3.customer_t3m_rev - c4.customer_p3m_rev) / nullif(c4.customer_p3m_rev,0))*100,2) < 0
		Then 'Declining'
		When Round(((c3.customer_t3m_rev - c4.customer_p3m_rev) / nullif(c4.customer_p3m_rev,0))*100,2) > 0 AND
			Round(((c3.customer_t3m_rev - c4.customer_p3m_rev) / nullif(c4.customer_p3m_rev,0))*100,2) < 5
		Then 'Steady'
		Else 'N/A'
	End momentum_status
From cte_2 c2
Left Join cte_3 c3
On c2.customer_code = c3.customer_code
Left Join cte_4 c4
On c2.customer_code = c4.customer_code
